<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="2">
  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="1"/><Text>INT. ARCHIVE BASEMENT - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Steel shelving to the ceiling. A single bulb, swinging.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="1"/><Text>EXT. LOADING DOCK - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Rain on corrugated tin, loud enough to argue over.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="1"/><Text>INT./EXT. DELIVERY VAN - MOVING - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The wipers lose.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="42"><SceneProperties Page="1"/><Text>INT. ARCHIVE BASEMENT - RESHELVING - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A dual-margin scene number, the shooting-script shape: the same number printed at both margins.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="2"/><Text>INT. READING ROOM - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>ODILE sets down a box that is heavier than it looks.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot"><Text>INDEX CARDS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Handwriting from four decades, none of it consistent.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot"><Text>LEDGER, LATER</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>One column, ruled in pencil, never once balanced.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>CUT TO:</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="2"/><Text>INT. STAIRWELL - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Footsteps going down two at a time.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>DISSOLVE TO:</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="2"/><Text>EXT. ARCHIVE - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The building keeps its lights on for nobody.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>SMASH CUT TO:</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="3"/><Text>INT. ARCHIVE BASEMENT - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Nobody is where their voice says they are.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(O.S.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>The period-full spelling, the one the manuals print.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(V.O)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>And the one writers actually type, missing its period.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(O.C)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Off camera, also missing its period.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>A continued cue, carrying its extension.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DR. E. T. MARCHETTI</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Dotted abbreviations sitting inside a character name.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>A hybrid: name and extension on one cue line.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="4"/><Text>INT. READING ROOM - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The box is open now. It was not worth the trip.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quietly)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>A leading parenthetical, before a word is spoken.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>A line, and then a beat in the middle of it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(reconsidering)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>And then the rest of it, after the beat.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(standing)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(then, to WREN)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Two stacked parentheticals before any dialogue at all.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="5"/><Text>INT. ARCHIVE BASEMENT - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They have been at this for six hours.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>No.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Yes.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>No.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>MORE-ANCHOR. This speech begins near the foot of the page on purpose, so that it runs over the break and has to be put back together on the other side. It keeps going well past the boundary so the rejoin has something substantial to work with, and so that the same speech doubles as the long-dialogue case the coverage table asks for, rather than spending two constructions on what is really one shape.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="7"/><Text>INT. CONSERVATION BENCH - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The label reads </Text><Text Style="Bold">DO NOT LAMINATE</Text><Text>, twice.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She says it </Text><Text Style="Italic">again</Text><Text>, and this time somebody writes it down.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The stamp is </Text><Text Style="Bold+Italic">both bold and italic</Text><Text> at once.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A styled run that </Text><Text Style="Bold">crosses the wrap boundary because it keeps</Text><Text> </Text><Text Style="Bold">going for long enough to need a second line</Text><Text>, and then stops.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Punctuation only, styled by itself.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>This word is </Text><Text Style="Underline">underlined</Text><Text> with drawn vector art.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>This phrase is struck through, above the baseline.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A table rules a border below this cell, further down.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A page-wide rule crosses this whole line of text.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>CHYRON: EVERY NAME HERE IS INVENTED.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A footnote, set smaller than the body.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The index card, enlarged for the reader.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A SIGN, VERY LARGE INDEED</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>A text message, in the phone’s own face.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Dialogue can be </Text><Text Style="Bold">bold</Text><Text> too.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>And </Text><Text Style="Italic">italic</Text><Text>, which is the common one.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="8"/><Text>INT. READING ROOM - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They speak over each other.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="General"><DualDialogue><Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph><Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>LEFTMARK. Short, on the left.</Text></Paragraph><Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph><Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>RIGHTMARK. Short, on the right.</Text></Paragraph></DualDialogue></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>And again, at length.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="General"><DualDialogue><Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph><Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>This column runs long enough that the taller of the two passes twelve estimated rendered lines, which is the threshold where the side-by-side table gives up and both speeches become ordinary sequential dialogue instead.</Text></Paragraph><Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph><Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>And this one answers at similar length so neither column is trivially short, because the fallback measures the taller of the pair and a stub would never reach it.</Text></Paragraph></DualDialogue></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech one. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech two. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech three. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech four. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech five. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech six. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech seven. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech eight. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech nine. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech ten. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech eleven. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twelve. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirteen. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech fourteen. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech fifteen. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech sixteen. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech seventeen. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech eighteen. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech nineteen. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-one. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-two. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-three. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-four. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-five. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-six. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-seven. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-eight. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech twenty-nine. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-one. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-two. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-three. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-four. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-five. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-six. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BUNNY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-seven. Short.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CASSIUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-eight. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ODILE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech thirty-nine. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Speech forty. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed. If this line sits alone at the top or the bottom of a page, the keep failed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="14"/><Text>INT. ART DEPARTMENT - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>WREN pins a storyboard panel to the wall, printed small.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WREN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Under half a column wide, and not a thumbnail.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="15"/><Text>INT. MAP ROOM - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><SceneProperties Page="16"/><Text>INT. FIRE STAIRS - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A production still, printed tall.</Text></Paragraph>
  </Content>
